"[2602.16100v1] LLM-Driven Intent-Based Privacy-Aware Orchestration Across the Cloud-Edge Continuum (https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.16100v1)\nciteturn29424view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.16100v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 18 Feb 2026]\nL9: # Title:LLM-Driven Intent-Based Privacy-Aware Orchestration Across the Cloud-Edge Continuum\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Zijie Su , cite6†Muhammed Tawfiqul Islam , cite7†Mohammad Goudarzi , cite8†Adel N. Toosi L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled LLM-Driven Intent-Based Privacy-Aware Orchestration Across the Cloud-Edge Continuum, by Zijie Su and 2 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite9†View PDF cite10†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:With the rapid advancement of large language models (LLMs), efficiently serving LLM inference under limited GPU resources has become a critical challenge. Recently, an increasing number of studies have explored applying serverless computing paradigms to LLM serving in order to maximize resource utilization.\nL17: However, LLM inference workloads are highly diverse, and modern GPU clusters are inherently heterogeneous, making it necessary to dynamically adjust deployment configurations online to better adapt to the elastic and dynamic nature of serverless environments. At the same time, enabling such online reconfiguration is particularly challenging due to the stateful nature of LLM inference and the massive size of model parameters.\nL18: In this paper, we propose a dynamic pipeline reconfiguration approach that enables online adjustment of pipeline configurations while minimizing service downtime and performance degradation. Our method allows the system to select the optimal pipeline configuration in response to changing workloads.\nL19: Experimental results on heterogeneous GPU platforms, including NVIDIA A100 and L40s, demonstrate that our migration mechanism incurs less than 50 ms of service downtime, while introducing under 10% overhead on both time-to-first-token (TTFT) and time-per-output-token (TPOT).\nL20: Subjects:  | Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing (cs.DC)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite11†arXiv:2602.16100 [cs.DC]\nL22:    | (or cite12†arXiv:2602.16100v1 [cs.DC] for this version)\nL23:    | cite13†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2602.16100†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: Journal reference:  | 24th Australasian Symposium on Parallel and Distributed Computing (AusPDC 2026)\nL25: Related DOI (Digital Object Identifier):  | cite14†https://doi.org/10.1145/3793811.3793824†doi.org DOI(s) linking to related resources\nL26: ## Submission history\nL27: \nL28: From: Muhammed Tawfiqul Islam [cite15†view email ]\nL29: [v1] Wed, 18 Feb 2026 00:09:09 UTC (4,559 KB)\nL30: \nL31: Full-text links:\nL32: \nL33: ## Access Paper:\nL34: \nL35: View a PDF of the paper titled LLM-Driven Intent-Based Privacy-Aware Orchestration Across the Cloud-Edge Continuum, by Zijie Su and 2 other authors\nL36: \nL37:   * cite9†View PDF L38:   * cite10†HTML (experimental) L39:   * cite16†TeX Source L40: \nL41: cite17†view license†creativecommons.org L42: ### Current browse context:\nL43: \nL44: cs.DC\nL45: \nL46: cite18†< prev |   cite19†next > L47: \nL48: cite20†new | cite21†recent | cite22†2026-02 L49: \nL50: Change to browse by:\nL51: \nL52: cite23†cs L53: \nL54: ### References & Citations\nL55: \nL56:   * cite24†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L57:   * cite25†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L58:   * cite26†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L59: \nL60: [Bu